{"title":"2022 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Super_fast!_No_algebra_and_no_testing_any_of_the_answer_choices!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Super fast! No algebra and no testing any of the answer choices!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀Super_Fast._Just_1_min!🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀Super Fast. Just 1 min!🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The grid below is to be filled with integers in such a way that the sum of the numbers in each row and the sum of the numbers in each column are the same. Four numbers are missing. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in the lower left corner is larger than the other three missing numbers. What is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71d1b8183aafd0b7db5af174a291282dccce49ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((3,3)--(-3,3)); draw((3,1)--(-3,1)); draw((3,-3)--(-3,-3)); draw((3,-1)--(-3,-1)); draw((3,3)--(3,-3)); draw((1,3)--(1,-3)); draw((-3,3)--(-3,-3)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,-3)); label((-2,2),&quot;$-2$&quot;); label((0,2),&quot;$9$&quot;); label((2,2),&quot;$5$&quot;); label((2,0),&quot;$-1$&quot;); label((2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((-2,-2),&quot;$x$&quot;); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a66570878657d0ede2e99f9e5acb25fdff246b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } -1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 9 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"411\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the numbers in each row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Consider the second row. In order for the sum of the numbers in this row to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the two shaded numbers must add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7bd639987ad1ac365aa9106b8977af7ed1d67f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); fill((-3,1)--(1,1)--(1,-1)--(-3,-1)--cycle,mediumgray); draw((3,3)--(-3,3)); draw((3,1)--(-3,1)); draw((3,-3)--(-3,-3)); draw((3,-1)--(-3,-1)); draw((3,3)--(3,-3)); draw((1,3)--(1,-3)); draw((-3,3)--(-3,-3)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,-3)); label((-2,2),&quot;$-2$&quot;); label((0,2),&quot;$9$&quot;); label((2,2),&quot;$5$&quot;); label((2,0),&quot;$-1$&quot;); label((2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((-2,-2),&quot;$x$&quot;); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\nIf two numbers add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, one of them must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: If both shaded numbers are no more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, their sum can be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be larger than the three missing numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can construct a working scenario where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf5d650726be49af3a306c54a2fd7dd1d628b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/634b125094f297b3a8e5e036f57c8b69a27a51b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((3,3)--(-3,3)); draw((3,1)--(-3,1)); draw((3,-3)--(-3,-3)); draw((3,-1)--(-3,-1)); draw((3,3)--(3,-3)); draw((1,3)--(1,-3)); draw((-3,3)--(-3,-3)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,-3)); label((-2,2),&quot;$-2$&quot;); label((0,2),&quot;$9$&quot;); label((2,2),&quot;$5$&quot;); label((2,0),&quot;$-1$&quot;); label((2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((-2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((0,-2),&quot;$-4$&quot;); label((-2,0),&quot;$6$&quot;); label((0,0),&quot;$7$&quot;); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\nSo, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7b13a4eb0160255f98d8da5a67b31a53dcf44bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ihatemath123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the numbers in each row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a2eb28de312372a5e8359a36fdbf4deea64a5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2+9+5=12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" /> and the sum of the numbers in each column is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b12baf731c5828bb43be5549720a4289ddeef0cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+(-1)+8=12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number in the lower middle. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c15cf665f5ce33b549ac69e89c5e6b47aed5ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+8=12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/657ebb9070e9b381330e64d18964a4106321e44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We express the other two missing numbers in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1d002db36c51a77f8fbc6314e96756fc793e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95efb3fbab86b4c09542f2a52d46080864821d0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((3,3)--(-3,3)); draw((3,1)--(-3,1)); draw((3,-3)--(-3,-3)); draw((3,-1)--(-3,-1)); draw((3,3)--(3,-3)); draw((1,3)--(1,-3)); draw((-3,3)--(-3,-3)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,-3)); label((-2,2),&quot;$-2$&quot;); label((0,2),&quot;$9$&quot;); label((2,2),&quot;$5$&quot;); label((2,0),&quot;$-1$&quot;); label((2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((-2,-2),&quot;$x$&quot;); label((0,-2),&quot;$y$&quot;,red+fontsize(11)); label((-2,0),&quot;$y{+}10$&quot;,red+fontsize(11)); label((0,0),&quot;$x{-}1$&quot;,red+fontsize(11));  [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aefbae79783df5f8e0fd8966df838dcdf10a6b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;x-1, x&gt;y+10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3da715357573df8bc1f1e715d72eb654f3ec417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> Note that the first inequality is true for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> We only need to solve the second inequality so that the third inequality is true for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> By substitution, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf48d867dee0c1758fef8ead76388375b75aee3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;(4-x)+10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6e6d9b003a0a2ff3884244dc2963dc10ae61de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841738515d2b311ea2079b59dc16a3eb488b9504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is based on the Solution 2 above and it is perhaps a little simpler than that.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number in the lower middle. Applying summation to first two columns yields the following.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0d36e2e04056562e036b4431a3419294aa1f58.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((3,3)--(-3,3)); draw((3,1)--(-3,1)); draw((3,-3)--(-3,-3)); draw((3,-1)--(-3,-1)); draw((3,3)--(3,-3)); draw((1,3)--(1,-3)); draw((-3,3)--(-3,-3)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,-3)); label((-2,2),&quot;$-2$&quot;); label((0,2),&quot;$9$&quot;); label((2,2),&quot;$5$&quot;); label((2,0),&quot;$-1$&quot;); label((2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((-2,-2),&quot;$x$&quot;); label((0,-2),&quot;$y$&quot;,red+fontsize(11)); label((-2,0),&quot;$14{-}x$&quot;,red+fontsize(11)); label((0,0),&quot;$3{-}y$&quot;,red+fontsize(11));  [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than the other three, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d3af8a30f9af3fe60f3c58dfb7f3ba33a5146fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;14-x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6e6d9b003a0a2ff3884244dc2963dc10ae61de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841738515d2b311ea2079b59dc16a3eb488b9504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~vetaltekdi6\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the sum of the rows and columns must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20d3344b0cef2bc9e9c7a7be3b84c6cb2dd9bd84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+5-1=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />. We proceed to test the answer choices.\n</p><p>Testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4c38a419ae56f13a202216dd45a1978bc91a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, the number above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which contradicts the precondition that the numbers surrounding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, the number above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which does not work.\n</p><p>Testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, the number above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which does not work.\n</p><p>Testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, the number above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which <i>does</i> work. Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced70e08fcbb7c9e3c5221a6a79e47dbc8637103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>We do not need to test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />, because the problem asks for the <b>smallest</b> value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Super_fast.21_No_algebra_and_no_testing_any_of_the_answer_choices.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Super_fast!_No_algebra_and_no_testing_any_of_the_answer_choices!)\">Solution 5 (Super fast! No algebra and no testing any of the answer choices!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Super fast! No algebra and no testing any of the answer choices!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the numbers in each column and row should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee102836cb04fbb91c92dc3783b68e8aec67ae0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+(-1)+8=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />. If we look at the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74534eea5b0e415e11f0266e494e0cb1cdf9da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{\\text{st}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> column, the gray squares (shown below) sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5ffba700d8415ce19ebab869187d67aeca32f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-(-2)=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b9246a027774ced6c90194b76ba316acd8e775.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((3,3)--(-3,3)); draw((3,1)--(-3,1)); draw((3,-3)--(-3,-3)); draw((3,-1)--(-3,-1)); draw((3,3)--(3,-3)); draw((1,3)--(1,-3)); draw((-3,3)--(-3,-3)); draw((-1,3)--(-1,-3)); label((-2,2),&quot;$-2$&quot;);    label((0,2),&quot;$9$&quot;); label((2,2),&quot;$5$&quot;); label((2,0),&quot;$-1$&quot;); label((2,-2),&quot;$8$&quot;); label((-2,-2),&quot;$x$&quot;); filldraw((-3,-3)--(-1,-3)--(-1,-1)--(-3,-1)--cycle, lightgray, black+linewidth(1)); filldraw((-1,-1)--(-3,-1)--(-3,1)--(-1,1)--cycle, lightgray, black+linewidth(1)); label(scale(1)*&quot;All credits for original unedited asymptote for the problem go to whoever made the asymptote in the &#39;Problem&#39; section.&quot;, (-0,-5), S); [/asy]\" width=\"1032\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><b>If</b> square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to be <b>greater than or equal to</b> the three blank squares, then the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be is half the sum of the value of the gray squares, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a06f0bbe2ea630270dae2a1e36a23825268502e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14\\div2=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. But square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to be <b>greater than</b> and <i><b>not</b></i> <b>greater than or equal to</b> the three blank squares, so the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d09375017769873b9c2c9ef474d76c91d14336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+1=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Testing for the other rows and columns (it might be smaller than the other two squares!), we find that the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be is indeed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; the other two squares are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/088ff9da520ce8f4ace3932970cda4fc8268c15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"53\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ JoyfulSapling\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oUEa7AjMF2A?si=Bbea8RWE2sMWN6xl&amp;t=3643\">https://youtu.be/oUEa7AjMF2A?si=Bbea8RWE2sMWN6xl&amp;t=3643</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tYWp6fcUAik?si=V8hv_zOn_zYOi9E5&amp;t=2489\">https://youtu.be/tYWp6fcUAik?si=V8hv_zOn_zYOi9E5&amp;t=2489</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80Super_Fast._Just_1_min.21.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀Super_Fast._Just_1_min!🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀Super Fast. Just 1 min!🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀Super Fast. Just 1 min!🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7J4EGPaB29Y\">https://youtu.be/7J4EGPaB29Y</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0hHlpIVeFjg\">https://youtu.be/0hHlpIVeFjg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xnGQffaxYAA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xnGQffaxYAA</a>\n</p><p>~Mathematical Dexterity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ij9pAy6tQSg?t=1857\">https://youtu.be/Ij9pAy6tQSg?t=1857</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hs6y4PWnoWg?t=369\">https://youtu.be/hs6y4PWnoWg?t=369</a>\n</p><p>~STEMbreezy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_5\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DXFwzrOF4b4\">https://youtu.be/DXFwzrOF4b4</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_6\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FINk9LgSJpU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FINk9LgSJpU</a>\n</p><p>~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]